  - The team's shared understanding is now that I (P1) have been given a clear signal to play. P2 expects me to play one of the clued cards on my upcoming turn.
  - My next action is now obvious: play either card 2 or card 4. A common convention is to play the oldest (left-most) playable card first, which would be card 2. This action will successfully start a firework and advance the game state.
  - The cards that were not clued (1, 3, 5) are now known to be non-1s. While they might be useful later, they are not immediately playable. They become lower priority and are now the primary candidates for discarding if the team needs to recover clue tokens in the future.

